Lab 11: Automating Ceph Management with Ansible
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand the fundamentals of Ansible automation for Ceph storage clusters
Write and execute Ansible playbooks for adding OSDs (Object Storage Daemons)
Automate the creation and configuration of Ceph pools using Ansible
Manage CRUSH map rules and understand how pools bind to specific CRUSH rules
Combine pool and CRUSH automation into a single reusable deployment playbook
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Ceph storage architecture and components (OSDs, monitors, pools, CRUSH)
Familiarity with Linux command line operations
Knowledge of YAML syntax and structure
Understanding of SSH key-based authentication
Previous experience with Ceph cluster operations (manual deployment preferred)
